{"case_id":"C064","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["serialization entry point","size-estimation state","floating-point input semantics"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["node_estimate_size","dtostr"],"reason":"H0 only parses inputs through plist_from_bin or plist_from_xml and then calls plist_free. It never exercises the serialization-side PLIST_REAL path in node_estimate_size, where S1 now calls dtostr(NULL, 0, data->realval). This size-only null-buffer protocol and its floating-point formatting behavior are therefore materially uncovered.","evidence":["bplist_fuzzer.cc calls only plist_from_bin followed by plist_free.","xplist_fuzzer.cc calls only plist_from_xml followed by plist_free.","The S1 change replaces the PLIST_REAL estimate in node_estimate_size with dtostr(NULL, 0, data->realval).","dtostr was changed to guard buffer access with `buf && i < len`, specifically enabling a NULL output buffer during size calculation.","PLIST_REAL values have distinct dtostr branches for infinity, zero, and general formatted values, none of which H0 drives through node_estimate_size."],"recommended_action":"Add a fuzz target or round-trip phase that sends plist trees containing PLIST_REAL nodes through the XML serialization path that invokes node_estimate_size and dtostr, covering finite values, very small and large values, signed zero, infinities, and size-only versus actual-output behavior."}
